Reduce to standard form:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\frac{36}{-24}$
    \item $\frac{-3}{-15}$
\end{enumerate}

pert_a:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item The HCF of 36 and 24 is 12. Thus, its standard form would be obtained by dividing by -12. \textcolor{red}{To confirm, we can also check that 36 is \(6 \times 6\) and -24 is \(-6 \times 4\), so the simplification holds.}
    \[
    \frac{36}{-24} = \frac{36 \div (-12)}{-24 \div (-12)} = \frac{-3}{2}
    \]

    \item The HCF of 3 and 15 is 3. Thus, \textcolor{red}{since -3 is a prime number,}
    \[
    \frac{-3}{-15} = \frac{-3 \div (-3)}{-15 \div (-3)} = \frac{1}{5}
    \]
\end{enumerate}

