 392 = 2 \times 2 \times 2 \times 7 \times 7

The prime factor 7 does not appear in a group of three. Therefore, 392 is not a perfect cube. To make it a cube, we need one more 7. In that case,

392 \times 7 = 2 \times 2 \times 2 \times 7 \times 7 \times 7 = 2744 \text{ which is a perfect cube.}

\textcolor{red}{Interestingly, the number 392 is also divisible by 4 and 98, but this fact does not affect whether it is a perfect cube.}


